,"factIds":["EDITORIAL74-018"],"major":"Art History","group":"Romanticism","stem":"In Romantic aesthetics, overwhelming nature that inspires awe and fear exemplifies what?","choices":["The grotesque","The picturesque","The idyllic","The sublime","The pastoral"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":"The sublime","explanation":"The sublime involves experiences of magnitude or power that may exceed calm, rational control.","format":"interpretation","references":[{"file":"Editorial reference: Romanticism","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://www.metmuseum.org/essays/romanticism"}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","version":"editorial-v76","editorialStatus74":"ready","skill74":"interpretation","topic74":"Romanticism","difficulty74":"unrated","lineage74":"Original editorial item; Alpha transcription used to benchmark concise options. Not an official CISIA question.","evidence":{"type":"editorial","referenceBasis":"Institutional reference","checkedAt":"2026-10-05"},"editorial75":{"sourceKey":"romanticism","optionWords":[2,2,2,2,2],"difficultyStatus":"Not calibrated with candidates","syllabusArea":"historical-cultural-space-time"},"fingerprint":"abd3051f2ba256019f09"},{"id":"GEN43-Q01019","qid":1019,"nodeId":"EDITORIAL74-019","relatedNodeIds":["EDITORIAL74-019"],"factIds":["EDITORIAL74-019"],"major":"Architecture","group":"Palladio","stem":"Which treatise helped disseminate Palladio’s architectural ideas?","choices":["The Seven Lamps of Architecture","Towards a New Architecture","The Ten Books on Architecture","The Four Books of Architecture","The Stones of Venice"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":"The Four Books of Architecture","explanation":"Palladio published I quattro libri dell’architettura in 1570; the similarly titled ten-book treatise is associated with Vitruvius.","format":"context","references":[{"file":"Editorial reference: Palladio","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/712/"}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","version":"editori