itution?","choices":["Parliament","Monarchy","Papacy","Universities","Guilds"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":"Monarchy","explanation":"Constitutional history involves successive developments; a medieval charter should not be equated with modern suffrage.","format":"comparison","references":[{"file":"Editorial reference: Magna Carta","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://www.parliament.uk/magnacarta/"}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","version":"editorial-v76","editorialStatus74":"ready","skill74":"comparison","topic74":"Magna Carta","difficulty74":"unrated","lineage74":"Original editorial item; Alpha transcription used to benchmark concise options. Not an official CISIA question.","evidence":{"type":"editorial","referenceBasis":"Institutional reference","checkedAt":"2026-10-05"},"editorial75":{"sourceKey":"magna","optionWords":[1,1,1,1,1],"difficultyStatus":"Not calibrated with candidates","syllabusArea":"historical-cultural-space-time"},"fingerprint":"457354fafaf4fbe82a57"},{"id":"GEN43-Q01077","qid":1077,"nodeId":"EDITORIAL74-077","relatedNodeIds":["EDITORIAL74-077"],"factIds":["EDITORIAL74-077"],"major":"Art History","group":"Ravenna","stem":"In a mosaic, the small individual pieces forming the image are called:","choices":["Tesserae","Metopes","Voussoirs","Coffers","Cartouches"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":"Tesserae","explanation":"Tesserae are the units of a mosaic; voussoirs are wedge-shaped elements of an arch.","format":"material","references":[{"file":"Editorial reference: Ravenna","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/708074"}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","version":"editorial-v76","editorialStatus74":"ready","skill74":"material","topic74":"Ravenna","difficulty74":"unrated","lineage74":"Original editorial item; Alpha transcription used to benchmark concise options. Not an official CISIA question.","evidence":{"type":"editorial","referenceBasis":"Institutional reference","checkedAt":"2026-10-0