rian monuments","difficulty74":"unrated","lineage74":"Original editorial item; Alpha transcription used to benchmark concise options. Not an official CISIA question.","evidence":{"type":"editorial","referenceBasis":"Existing dated record","checkedAt":"2026-10-05"},"editorial75":{"sourceKey":"timeline:Equestrian statue of Gattamelata","optionWords":[2,2,3,2,3],"difficultyStatus":"Not calibrated with candidates","syllabusArea":"historical-cultural-space-time","tapestryRecordId":"t63-e096d6497e4f"},"fingerprint":"59797474905261908585","imageId":"PHOTO100-t63-e096d6497e4f","imageDependency":"helpful","mediaReview100":"exact source article for the work"},{"id":"GEN43-Q01208","qid":1208,"nodeId":"EDITORIAL76-208","relatedNodeIds":["EDITORIAL76-208"],"factIds":["EDITORIAL76-208"],"major":"Architecture","group":"Florentine palaces","stem":"Michelozzo’s Palazzo Medici was originally built for whom?","choices":["Lorenzo the Magnificent","Cosimo I de’ Medici","Ferdinando I de’ Medici","Giuliano de’ Medici","Cosimo de’ Medici"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":"Cosimo de’ Medici","explanation":"Cosimo the Elder commissioned the palace; the Riccardi later extended it.","format":"patronage","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record: Palazzo Medici Riccardi","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palazzo_Medici_Riccardi"}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","version":"editorial-v76","editorialStatus74":"ready","skill74":"patronage","topic74":"Florentine palaces","difficulty74":"unrated","lineage74":"Original editorial item; Alpha transcription used to benchmark concise options. Not an official CISIA question.","evidence":{"type":"editorial","referenceBasis":"Existing dated record","checkedAt":"2026-10-05"},"editorial75":{"sourceKey":"timeline:Palazzo Medici Riccardi","optionWords":[3,4,4,3,3],"difficultyStatus":"Not calibrated with candidates","syllabusArea":"historical-cultural-space-time","tapestryRecordId":"t63-d1a7f4612e0d"},"fingerprint":"35b67cfd