os"}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","version":"editorial-v76","editorialStatus74":"ready","skill74":"observation","topic74":"Dürer","difficulty74":"unrated","lineage74":"Original editorial item; Alpha transcription used to benchmark concise options. Not an official CISIA question.","evidence":{"type":"editorial","referenceBasis":"Existing dated record","checkedAt":"2026-10-05"},"editorial75":{"sourceKey":"timeline:Rhinoceros","optionWords":[3,3,2,3,3],"difficultyStatus":"Not calibrated with candidates","syllabusArea":"historical-cultural-space-time","tapestryRecordId":"t63-7c5e9722d627"},"fingerprint":"be4f1118e61b3944f906","imageId":"PHOTO100-t63-7c5e9722d627","imageDependency":"helpful","mediaReview100":"exact source article for the work"},{"id":"GEN43-Q01222","qid":1222,"nodeId":"EDITORIAL76-222","relatedNodeIds":["EDITORIAL76-222"],"factIds":["EDITORIAL76-222"],"major":"Art History","group":"Andrea del Sarto","stem":"The title Madonna of the Harpies refers to figures on which part of the painting?","choices":["Heavenly vault","Altarpiece frame","Pedestal","Virgin’s mantle","Landscape horizon"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":"Pedestal","explanation":"The unusual creatures decorate the pedestal beneath the Virgin.","format":"iconography","references":[{"file":"Tapestry source record: Madonna of the Harpies","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madonna_of_the_Harpies"}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","version":"editorial-v76","editorialStatus74":"ready","skill74":"iconography","topic74":"Andrea del Sarto","difficulty74":"unrated","lineage74":"Original editorial item; Alpha transcription used to benchmark concise options. Not an official CISIA question.","evidence":{"type":"editorial","referenceBasis":"Existing dated record","checkedAt":"2026-10-05"},"editorial75":{"sourceKey":"timeline:Madonna of the Harpies","optionWords":[2,2,1,2,2],"difficultyStatus":"Not calibrated with candidates","syllabusArea":"historical-cultu